# Canonicalization

Environment: NixOS with Nix flakes and preservation. HOME is a Git repository containing flake-enabled Git submodules in Go-style paths. Each submodule follows a subset of the numtide/blueprint directory structure.

# Initialize HOME
# Create the empty project remote
git_canonicalization init home
# Add required home whitelist entries in .gitignore
# Stage files before cleanup

# Initialize repository
git_canonicalization init flake git@github.com:owner/demo.git

# Add package
cd "$HOME/github.com/owner/demo"
git_canonicalization add python demo "A demo package."

# Remove package
cd "$HOME/github.com/owner/demo"
git_canonicalization rm demo

# Enter a package's development environment
cd "$HOME/github.com/owner/demo"
nix develop .#package-name

# Run a local package
cd "$HOME/github.com/owner/demo"
nix run .#package-name

# Run a package from the registry
nix run nixpkgs#package-name

# Format, build, and test packages and hosts
nix fmt
nix flake check

# Run a command in each HOME submodule
cd
git submodule foreach <command> # e.g. nix fmt, nix flake check

# Rules
# Use Nix flakes in repositories
# Use git_canonicalization for all persistent directory-structure changes; use prm/ for exceptions
# Keep as few files and directories as possible in prm/
# Save generated artifacts in tmp/ directories
